<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A2.SS2" title="In Appendix B Derivation of the Lagrangian and the 𝛽-ϵ Correspondence ‣ WaterVIB: Learning Minimal Sufficient Watermark Representations via Variational Information Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">B.2 </span>Lagrangian Construction</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A2.SS3" title="In Appendix B Derivation of the Lagrangian and the 𝛽-ϵ Correspondence ‣ WaterVIB: Learning Minimal Sufficient Watermark Representations via Variational Information Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">B.3 </span>Step 3: Geometry of the Solution and Strict Convexity</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A2.SS4" title="In Appendix B Derivation of the Lagrangian and the 𝛽-ϵ Correspondence ‣ WaterVIB: Learning Minimal Sufficient Watermark Representations via Variational Information Bottleneck" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">B.4 </span>Step 4: Proof of the Bijective Mapping (<math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\leftrightarrow\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">↔</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\leftrightarrow\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
